<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at Brazil's Santos port.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at Brazil's Santos port.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santos port reported the following conditions for shipments of soybeans and soymeal:</p>
<p>Vessels: Irawady loading 57,750 tonnes soybeans. Hilon of Sparta waiting to dock, to load 55,000 soybeans. Mentese waiting to dock to complete loading of 45,000 tonnes soybeans begun last week. Rover waiting to dock, to load 43,000 soybeans. At Cargill private terminal, Merinee still loading 32,000 tonnes soymeal, expected to leave 1700 local (200 GMT). No other vessel programmed.</p>
<p>Road: 299 trucks arrived on Monday unloading 7,816 tonnes soybeans.</p>
<p>Rail: 19 wagons arrived unloading 1,016 tonnes soybeans. 15 wagons arrived unloading 802 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>Stocks: 112,311 tonnes soybeans, 387 tonnes soymeal.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
